course: dictionary
lesson: 9198
title: Softening words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Soften is a verb, an action word. It tells you what something does or what happens to it. It has two main meanings. The first is to become softer, or to make something softer: «soften the butter» means make the butter soft so it spreads easily.
explain: The second meaning is to become or make something gentler, kinder or less strong. «Soften the blow» means make a hit, or bad news, easier to take. «Her face softened» means her cross look became kinder.
explain: To work out which meaning fits, look at the words around soften. If the sentence is about heat, a kitchen or a material, it probably means make softer. If it is about a voice, a face or a feeling, it probably means gentler or kinder.
fact: Soften is a verb: soften, softens, softened, softening.
fact: «Soften» means to become softer, or to make something softer.
fact: «Soften» can also mean to become gentler, kinder or less strong.
fact: Heat softens butter and chocolate, and water softens clay.
fact: People soften their words to be kind, so «soften the blow» means make bad news easier to take.
exercise: «Sand, mats and the foam in a helmet soften a blow by letting you stop more slowly.» What does soften mean in this sentence? | *Make less hard | Make much harder | Paint in bright colours | Dry out completely
exercise: «Leave the butter out for an hour so it will soften.» What does soften mean here? | *Become softer | Freeze solid | Shrink to half its size | Turn into a stone
exercise: «Her face softened when the puppy licked her hand.» What does softened mean? | Fell asleep | Turned bright red | Became harder and colder | *Became kinder and gentler
test: «Dad's voice softened when he saw how sorry I was.» What does softened mean? | *Became gentler | Became louder | Got angrier | Stopped talking
test: Which word means to make something softer or gentler? | Harden | Shrink | Freeze | *Soften
exam: Dad says, «I will soften the news for you.» What does soften mean? | *Make it gentler and easier to hear | Write it down in capitals | Forget it completely | Make it louder and more shocking
